{{! Watermark Remover. The scope note is deliberate and prominent: overlay
    watermarks come off losslessly, but content hidden beneath a raster stamp
    cannot be recovered without inventing it. Saying so up front is the only
    honest option for documents that carry legal weight. }}
<div class="page-head"><h1>Watermark Remover</h1></div>

<div class="notice info">
  <strong>What this can and cannot do.</strong> Watermarks added as a separate
  layer - text, annotations or optional-content groups - are removed
  <strong>losslessly</strong>: the page keeps its original fonts, tables, images
  and layout exactly. A watermark burned into a scanned image is different: the
  pixels underneath were never captured, so anything placed there can only be
  guessed. Those pages are marked <span class="badge mono review">LOSSY</span>
  and the original is always kept.
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="dropzone" id="wm-dropzone">
    <div class="big">Upload PDF Files</div>
    <div class="btn-row" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:12px">
      <button class="btn-primary" id="btn-wm-browse">Browse PDFs</button>
    </div>
    <div class="hint">Originals are never modified. Cleaned copies are written
      into a <strong>{{subfolder}}</strong> folder beside them.</div>
  </div>
</div>

{{! Where the results go, shown before the run as well as after - an operator
    should not have to clean a folder of deeds to find out where the copies
    landed. One folder per source folder, since a selection can span several. }}
{{#has_files}}
<div class="notice info">
  <strong>Cleaned copies will be saved to</strong>
  {{^many_outputs}}<code>{{output_dir}}</code>{{/many_outputs}}
  {{#many_outputs}}
  <span>these folders, one beside each folder of deeds you chose:</span>
  <ul style="margin:6px 0 0 18px">
    {{#output_dirs}}<li><code>{{path}}</code></li>{{/output_dirs}}
  </ul>
  {{/many_outputs}}
</div>
{{/has_files}}

{{#has_files}}
<div class="card">
  <h2>Selected Files</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>File</th><th class="num">Pages</th><th>Detected</th>
        <th>Method</th><th>Result</th><th>Saved to / Reason</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {{#files}}
        <tr>
          <td>{{name}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{pages}}</td>
          <td>{{#detected}}<span class="badge {{detect_class}}">{{detected}}</span>{{/detected}}
              {{^detected}}<span class="muted">not scanned</span>{{/detected}}</td>
          <td>{{method}}</td>
          <td>{{#done}}<span class="badge {{result_class}}">{{result}}</span>{{/done}}
              {{^done}}<span class="muted">pending</span>{{/done}}</td>
          <td class="script">
            {{#output}}<code>{{output}}</code>{{/output}}
            {{! The existing reason display: whatever the remover said, in full,
                never a bare "failed". }}
            {{#reason}}{{reason}}{{/reason}}
          </td>
        </tr>
      {{/files}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
{{/has_files}}

{{#has_run}}
<div class="card tight">
  <h2>Progress</h2>
  <div class="progress-row">
    <span class="name">Processed</span>
    <span class="bar"><span style="width:{{percent}}%"></span></span>
    <span class="count">{{done}} / {{total}} &middot; {{percent}}%</span>
  </div>
  <div class="tiles" style="margin-top:14px">
    <div class="tile violet"><div class="value">{{total}}</div><div class="label">Selected</div></div>
    <div class="tile ok"><div class="value">{{cleaned}}</div><div class="label">Cleaned</div></div>
    <div class="tile danger"><div class="value">{{failed}}</div><div class="label">Failed</div></div>
  </div>
</div>
{{/has_run}}

<div class="btn-row">
  <button class="btn-primary" id="btn-wm-scan" {{^has_files}}disabled{{/has_files}}>Detect Watermarks</button>
  <button class="btn-secondary" id="btn-wm-remove" {{^can_remove}}disabled{{/can_remove}}>Remove Watermarks</button>
  <button id="btn-wm-open" {{^has_output}}disabled{{/has_output}}>Open Output Folder</button>
  <button id="btn-wm-clear">Clear</button>
</div>

<div class="card tight" style="margin-top:16px">
  <h2>Detection Methods</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>How it is removed</th><th>Fidelity</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Optional content group (OCG)</td>
            <td class="script">The layer is dropped from the page tree.</td>
            <td><span class="badge ok">Lossless</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Annotation / stamp</td>
            <td class="script">The annotation object is deleted.</td>
            <td><span class="badge ok">Lossless</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Vector or text overlay</td>
            <td class="script">Matching drawing operators are removed from the content stream.</td>
            <td><span class="badge ok">Lossless</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Raster, burned into a scan</td>
            <td class="script">Inpainting estimates the covered pixels. Text underneath may not be recoverable.</td>
            <td><span class="badge review">Lossy</span></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
